   "ocr_text": "BACK-TO-WORK Pumping Checklist\nA simple one-page plan for\nyour workday pumping routine\nMomcozy × Aeroflow Breastpumps | Melissa Kotlen, RN, IBCLC I\nSarah Van Zandt, IBCLC, PMH-C\n1. Before Your First Day Back\nTest your pumping setup before the first\nworkweek.\n口\nConfirm that pumping feels comfortable\nand your flange fit works for you.\nKnow your pump parts, charger/power\nsource, and basic setup.\nIdentify when and where you can\nrealistically pump during your workday.\nPlan around your baby's usual feeding\npattern, your time apart, and your\navailable work breaks.\nCheck what workplace pumping\nprotections and space may apply to you.\n3. Have A Backup Plan\nKnow one backup option if your pump\ndoes not cooperate.\n• Consider hand expression or a backup\nmanual pump.\nKeep extra pump parts at work or in\nyour bag.\nL\nJ\nCarry a spare charger or power cord.\nIf safe milk storage is not available,\nkeep prioritizing comfort and regular\nmilk removal.\n2. Pack Your Pump-At-Work Bag\n• Pump + charger or power source\nCorrect-fit flanges or inserts\nBottles or milk storage bags\nL\nCooler bag + frozen ice packs, if needed\nSpare parts for the pieces most likely to\nget lost or fail\n口\nLabels or a simple tracking system\nNursing pads + an extra shirt\nWater + snack\n4. Keep The Routine Flexible\n口\nAim for regular milk removal—not\nperfect timing\nIf baby feeds before you leave, adjust\nthe timing of your first pump.\nIf meetings or breaks shift, adjust the\nremaining sessions as needed.\nA shorter session can still provide some\nmilk removal and relief when time is\nlimited.\nAvoid making skipped milk removals\nyour regular pattern.\nKeep it simple: the best routine is one you can actually repeat on a real workday.\nPlanning aid based on the Momcozy × Aeroflow Breast Pumps Webinar. Individual routines and needs vary.\nmomcoZy | Aeroflow,\nBreastpumps",
